      "writtenOn": "2023-02-21T16:01:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The test callback isn\u0027t very well suited for testing the callback logic itself, which is what these tests are doing. It also behaves incorrectly when you use a direct executor (as the thread that runs the callbacks is different between initialization from the test and the callback execution). \n\nSo as a result, I\u0027m using a custom callback so the specifics of those few tests don\u0027t leak elsewhere and make the TestUrlRequestCallback overly generic.",
      "parentUuid": "ca8ed4bd_4ebbb662",
      "revId": "c1bd2c9fd4e972f95af385321fef12008f7d9350",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
